body:
The story decorator writes/removes `sessionStorage` keys without guarding against storage being unavailable (the app code already treats this as possible, e.g. Safari private browsing). Wrap the `setItem`/`removeItem` calls in try/catch so Storybook doesn’t crash in those environments.
```suggestion
      actionableServiceIds.forEach((id) => {
        try {
          sessionStorage.setItem(`${CONTACT_REQUEST_SESSION_KEY_PREFIX}${id}`, 'true');
        } catch {
          // Ignore storage failures so Storybook still renders in restricted environments.
        }
      });

      try {
        return <Story />;
      } finally {
        actionableServiceIds.forEach((id) => {
          try {
            sessionStorage.removeItem(`${CONTACT_REQUEST_SESSION_KEY_PREFIX}${id}`);
          } catch {
            // Ignore storage failures so Storybook cleanup doesn't crash rendering.
          }
        });
```

test name : shows Basic and Public Preview badges when unlicensed
description : Verifies that File IQ shows "Basic" and Ops IQ shows "Public Preview" in the NoServicesLicensed scenario.

So assertions only verify that the text appears somewhere on the page. They don't verify the service.

So check, is it required to add like this or not :

const fileIqCard = page.getByRole('button', { name: /File IQ/ });
const opsIqCard  = page.getByRole('button', { name: /Ops IQ/ });

await expect.element(fileIqCard.getByText('Basic')).toBeVisible();
await expect.element(opsIqCard.getByText('Public Preview')).toBeVisible();
